      "writtenOn": "2022-11-28T19:32:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The patch the parent CL of this one was trying to revert was not an ideal fix for the issue it was trying to tackle. The problem was: specific headsets that rely on the host to expose the AVRCP Control profiles to connect correctly. The following if statement don\u0027t have an else arm. So a stack with is_new_avrcp_enabled() will not register the SDP record for AVRCP control.\n```\nif (profile_initialized \u003d\u003d UUID_SERVCLASS_AUDIO_SOURCE \u0026\u0026!is_new_avrcp_enabled())\n```\n\nIn the meantime, the original patch may duplicate the registration if the stack is not is_new_avrcp_enabled(). It will register for AVRCP control at init time and here.",
